      "confidence": "high",
      "rationale": "L5 explicitly names Thr-120 as the insertion site and confirms extracellular display by protease sensitivity in intact oocytes. Python confirms T120 (residue 120 = T) in the canonical sequence, within EC2 (116\u2013135), 5 residues from the TM3 C-boundary (115) and 16 residues from the TM4 N-boundary (136), satisfying the \u22653-residue TM clearance requirement. 'Inserted at Thr-120' is interpreted as insert_after_residue=120 (tag between T120 and G121), placing the tag mid-loop with ample flanking space. A coronavirus E1 glycoprotein epitope was inserted at Thr-120 of full-length CHIP/AQP1 expressed in Xenopus oocytes. Protease (alpha-chymotrypsin) sensitivity in intact oocytes confirmed extracellular display of the epitope at this position, establishing loop C (EC2, residues 116\u2013135) as exofacial.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 7507481,
          "citation": "PMID 7507481",
          "claim": "An epitope from the coronavirus E1 glycoprotein was inserted into CHIP and localized to the outer or inner leaflet of the membrane by alpha-chymotrypsin digestion of intact oocytes or inside-out membrane vesicles. The E1 epitope at Thr-120 was protease-sensitive in intact oocytes, indicating that loop C is exofacial. The E1 epitope at Lys-6, Arg-162, or Lys-267 was protease-sensitive in inside-out membrane vesicles, confirming the cytoplasmic location of the NH2 and COOH termini and loop D."
